+# Agent Note: Register Repository-External Session Event Owners
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-08-28-repository-external-session-event-registration.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+A package distributed outside this repository can declaration-merge `SessionEventMap` and append required durable facts, but the generated `KNOWN_SESSION_EVENT_TYPES` set contains only declarations visible to this repository's build. The live process can therefore write a type that the same composition refuses after restart. Treating the record as optional would lose plugin state silently, while accepting every unknown type would let the runtime resume without understanding facts that can affect later model input or policy.
+
+Runtime composition must decide whether the required owner is present. That decision must remain effect-scoped: hot removal of the owner cannot leave a stale cold-session preparation authorized by an earlier registration, and two unrelated packages cannot claim the same event semantics.
+
+## Decision
+
+`SessionStore.registerEventType(type, packageName)` registers one repository-external required-on-read event type for the lifetime of the calling effect. The first registration records the package owner; repeated registrations from the same package are reference-counted, and disposing the last registration removes recognition. An empty or padded package name, a claim for a generated first-party type, or a claim that conflicts with another package fails at registration.
+
+The persistence reader recognizes the union of generated first-party event types and live external registrations. Every other type still fails with `SessionFormatUnsupportedError`. The diagnostic directs the operator to install or enable the owning plugin, or upgrade the Harness when a newer build wrote the event. Registration does not make an event optional, load its package, validate its payload, or replace the owner's `SessionEventMap` declaration and invariant companion.
+
+`PersistenceCoordinator` records the external-event registration revision on each prepared cold source. Before it reuses that preparation, it revalidates all stored event types when the revision changed. A removed plugin therefore cannot borrow an accepted preparation from the composition that previously mounted it.
+
+Registration is runtime composition state only. It adds no field to `SessionEvent`, JSONL, SQLite, session transport, or the generated first-party event catalog; `SESSION_FORMAT_VERSION` remains `0`.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Mark repository-external events ignorable.** Rejected because the motivating events carry required plugin state. Skipping one can change later prompts, projections, or policy without a diagnostic.
+
+**Accept every declaration-merged type automatically.** Rejected because TypeScript declarations are erased and the external package is not part of this repository's generated program. Static typing proves an append call within a compilation, not that the current runtime mounted an interpreter for stored semantics.
+
+**Accept a type whenever its package is installed.** Rejected because installation does not prove that the plugin is enabled, initialized successfully, or owns that type. An explicit registration is the smallest runtime proof and gives Cordis effect disposal a precise lifecycle.
+
+**Persist a package owner on every event envelope.** Rejected because ownership is needed to authorize the current reader, not to interpret each record. Expanding every backend and transport would change the on-disk format without removing the need for a live interpreter registration.
+
+## Consequences
+
+An external package that persists a required event must register every such type before a cold session is loaded. A matching composition resumes the event losslessly; a missing, disabled, or conflicting owner fails loudly instead of degrading the session. Multiple instances of one package can share ownership without unloading each other, while different packages cannot assign competing semantics to one name.
+
+First-party event generation and storage bytes remain unchanged. The registration revision makes cached preparation reuse composition-safe at the cost of one complete event-type scan after the recognized external set changes.
+
+Focused SessionStore tests pin registration, duplicate ownership, conflict refusal, first-party refusal, and effect disposal. The shared JSONL and SQLite coordinator contract pins success only while an owner is registered and failure after removal or restart. The assembled Loader test restores a required external event through a real mounted fixture, while the existing assembled refusal path pins the actionable missing-owner diagnostic and raw artifact path.
